In view of the aforesaid discussion, this writ petition is disposed of on the following conditions:-
(i) The petitioner herein shall submit an undertaking along with an affidavit in C.C.No.185 of 2022, pending on the file of the Court of the Judicial First Class Magistrate at Metpalli, stating that he shall not leave India during pendency of the said C.C. without permission of the Court and that he shall co-operate with trial Court in concluding the proceedings in the said C.C.
(ii) On filing such an undertaking as well as an affidavit, the trial Court shall issue certified copy of the same within two (02) weeks therefrom;
(iii) The petitioner herein shall submit an application afresh along with certified copy of this order as well as the aforesaid undertaking before the Passport Officer/
Authority concerned for renewal of his passport;
(iv) On filing such an application, respondent No.2, the Passport Officer/Authority shall consider the same afresh in the light of the observations made by this Court as well as the contents of the undertaking given by the petitioner for renewal of his passport, in accordance with law, within three (03) weeks from the date of said application;
(v) On renewal of the Passport, the petitioner herein shall deposit the original renewed passport before the trial Court in C.C.No.185 of 2022;
(vi) However, liberty is granted to the petitioner herein to file an application before the learned Magistrate seeking permission to travel abroad, and it is for him to consider the same, in accordance with law.

